      "title": "Opening",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 18.646,
      "transcript": "Welcome to Small Hours, a short conversation about making room for creative work. Today we are looking at the moments between the big milestones: the first rough sketch, the question that changes a project, and the small decision to try again. This is an original synthetic audio fixture for an interface demonstration."
    },
    {
      "id": "chapter-2",
      "title": "The working draft",
      "start": 19.146,
      "end": 36.047,
      "transcript": "A working draft is a way to think in public. It gives a team something specific to question. Instead of asking whether an idea is good, we can ask what it helps someone do, where it becomes confusing, and which detail deserves another pass. The most useful review makes the next decision clearer."
    },
    {
      "id": "chapter-3",
      "title": "Closing",
      "start": 36.547,
      "end": 52.818,
      "transcript": "Before we wrap up, choose one small thing to improve in the next version. Keep the parts that already work. Leave a note explaining what changed and why. Then give the new version enough room to surprise you. Thanks for spending a few quiet minutes with Small Hours. We will see you next time."
    }
  ],
